\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Join all the glorious names
\par Of wisdom, love, and power,
\par That ever mortals knew,
\par That angels ever bore;
\par All are too mean to speak His worth,
\par Too mean to set our Saviour forth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. But O what gentle means,
\par What condescending ways,
\par Doth our Redeemer use,
\par To teach His heavenly grace;
\par My soul, with joy and wonder see
\par What forms of love He bears for thee!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Arrayed in mortal flesh
\par The Covenant Angel stands,
\par And holds the promises
\par And pardons in His hands;
\par Commissioned from His Father's throne
\par To make His grace to mortals known.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Great Prophet of my God,
\par My tongue would bless Thy name:
\par By Thee the joyful news 
\par Of our salvation came;
\par The joyful news of sins forgiven,
\par Of hell subdued, and peace with heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Be Thou my Counsellor,
\par My Pattern, and my Guide;
\par And through this desert land
\par Still keep me near Thy side:
\par O let my feet ne'er run astray,
\par Nor rove, nor seek the crooked way!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. I love my Shepherd's voice;
\par His watchful eye shall keep
\par My wandering soul among
\par The thousands of His sheep:
\par He feeds His flock, He calls their names,
\par Bears in His arms the tender lambs.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Jesus, my great High-priest,
\par Offered His blood and died;
\par My guilty conscience seeks
\par No sacrifice beside;
\par His powerful blood did once atone,
\par And now it pleads before the throne.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. O Thou Almighty Lord,
\par My Conquerer and my King,
\par Thy sceptre and Thy sword,
\par Thy reign of grace, I sing;
\par Thine is the power: behold I sit
\par In willing bonds before Thy feet.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9. Now let my soul arise,
\par And tread the tempter down:
\par My Captain leads me forth
\par To conquest and a crown:
\par March on, nor fear to win the day,
\par Though death and hell obstruct the way.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10. Should all the hosts of death,
\par And powers of hell unknown,
\par Put their most dreadful forms 
\par Of rage and malice on,
\par I shall be safe; for Christ displays
\par Superior power and guardian grace.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

